{
  "kanji": "面",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 面\ntitle: surface; mask\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-3, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 9\nradical: 面\nradicalNumber: 176\nonyomi: [メン, ベン]\nkunyomi: [おも, おもて, つら]\ndistractors: [目, 百, 同]\n---\n\n# 面 — surface; mask\n\n**Strokes:** 9 · **Key (radical):** 面 (no. 176) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n面 can mean a face, mask, or surface. 表面 (ひょうめん) names a surface or exterior.\nIn [面白い](../words/面白い.md) おもしろい, however, learn the whole adjective meaning \"interesting\";\n\"white face\" is not a usable translation of it.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** imagine the inner upright strokes as a face framed by the broad outer enclosure.\nThis is a visual memory aid, not a reconstruction of the character's origin.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| メン | on | 表面 ひょうめん — surface |\n| おも | kun | [面白い](../words/面白い.md) おもしろい — interesting |\n\nOther source readings remain in the metadata; these examples do not illustrate them all.\n\n## Common words\n\n- [面白い](../words/面白い.md) おもしろい — interesting; also amusing\n- 表面 ひょうめん — surface; exterior\n\n## Notes\n\n[顔](顔.md) focuses on the face in words such as 顔 (かお); 面 also covers surfaces and masks.\nBoth characters can mean \"face,\" though their uses depend on the word.\nDistinguish the inner arrangement from [目](目.md), the top and enclosure from [百](百.md),\nand the inner 口 shape of [同](同.md).\n\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1489880, 1533580.\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\n",
